! GAPS deck: StorageController seasonal targets (Get_DynamicTarget) —
! deterministic. Seasons/SeasonTargets + Set SeasonRating=yes and a
! SeasonSignal XYcurve mapping intHour -> season index select the kW target.
! The curve holds flat at Y=1 from hour 12 on (a 3rd point repeats the Y=1
! ordinate) rather than extrapolating past it: the live-oracle harness issues
! additional bare `solve` commands after this deck's own `Solve` (mode=daily
! is sticky, so each extends the run another `number=24` hours), and an
! unbounded linear extrapolation would eventually truncate to exactly
! `Seasons` (2) — Pascal `Get_DynamicTarget`'s `RatingIdx <= Seasons` guard
! (off-by-one; see StorageController.pas l.1033) then indexes SeasonTargets
! one past its valid `0..Seasons-1` range, an upstream dynamic-array OOB read
! that made the PINNED ORACLE itself hang at Max Control Iterations (#485)
! reading garbage. Held flat, RatingIdx never leaves {0, 1} no matter how far
! the harness re-drives.
Clear
New Circuit.gaps_scs basekv=12.47 phases=3 bus1=sourcebus mvasc3=200 mvasc1=210
New Loadshape.day8 npts=8 interval=3 mult=(0.40 0.55 0.75 0.95 1.00 0.90 0.70 0.50)
New XYcurve.seasonsig npts=3 xarray=(0 12 24) yarray=(0 1 1)
New Line.l1 bus1=sourcebus bus2=b1 phases=3 r1=0.30 x1=0.90 r0=0.9 x0=2.7 c1=3.0 c0=1.5 length=2 units=km
New Load.ld1 bus1=b1 phases=3 kv=12.47 kw=900 pf=0.95 model=1 daily=day8
New Storage.batt bus1=b1 phases=3 kv=12.47 kva=400 kwrated=350 kwhrated=1400 %stored=80 %reserve=20 state=idling dispmode=external
New StorageController.sc element=Line.l1 terminal=1 elementlist=[batt] modedischarge=peakshave kwtarget=700 modecharge=time timechargetrigger=2 %ratecharge=40 seasons=2 seasontargets=(700 500) seasontargetslow=(300 200) eventlog=yes
Set SeasonRating=yes
Set SeasonSignal=seasonsig
Set voltagebases=[12.47]
Calcvoltagebases
Set maxcontroliter=200
Set mode=daily stepsize=1h number=24
Solve
